From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Wed, 02 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman: pcd: hybrid EKFC+GEC CC-tree isolating experiment (T-M6-8 VLAN-v6 V6-2c)

install_v6 and install_v4gec (0186/0187, both board-tested 2026-09-02)
proved F-236's all-GEC dual-lane scheme (KGSE_EKFC forced to 0, GEC
words written) reprograms the KeyGen scheme correctly at the register
level, but a real, confirmed-arriving matching frame still misses the
CC-tree comparator -- for BOTH IPv4 and IPv6, under identical EKFC=0
machinery. That's a clean, family-independent negative result: the
gap is EKFC=0 sourcing itself, not v6-specific GEC codes or key width.

A qdrant/RM alignment review found the likely reason: this project's
own F-190 (2026-08-31) established the CC comparator's behavior is
sensitive to the scheme's EKFC value specifically, and the vendor
never ships an EKFC=0 all-GEC scheme in production -- every real
vendor scheme carries EKFC for known fields, GEC only as a fallback.
F-224's all-GEC design was this project's own invention for the
EHASH/FE-VM path and had never been exercised against the CC-tree
comparator before this week.

This adds the OTHER half of that hypothesis test: keep KGSE_EKFC
nonzero (KG_SCH_KN_PORT_ID alone, 0x80000000 -- the single known
field F-183/F-190 already established extracts a deterministic 0x00
byte on this ucode) instead of zeroing it, via the new
fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual_ekfc() (companion fixup F-238,
bin/kernel-fixups/F_238.py, widens F-236's kgse_ekfc=0 branch behind
a new gec_keep_ekfc flag). Because "generic extracts APPEND after
known EKFC fields" (vendor source), a nonzero-EKFC composite is ONE
BYTE WIDER than the all-GEC one, not the same width with different
content -- so this adds a separate cc_pack_key_dual_pid() packer
(47 bytes: PORT_ID byte 0, then the existing 46-byte dual-lane layout
shifted +1) rather than touching the proven cc_pack_key_dual().

New surface:
  - fman_pcd_cc.c: cc_pack_key_dual_pid(), CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID (47),
    wired into fman_pcd_cc_static_install() behind
    struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec.dual_lane_pid (only meaningful when
    dual_lane is also set; false for every existing caller, so
    install_vlan/install_v6/install_v4gec are byte-identical).
  - fman_pcd.h: dual_lane_pid field + declaration for
    fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual_ekfc() (defined by fixup F-238,
    fman_pcd_kg.c).
  - fman_pcd_cc_test.c: new "install_v6pid <port> <proto> <src-ip6>
    <dst-ip6> <sport> <dport> <fqid-hex>" debugfs verb, identical to
    install_v6 except it arms the hybrid EKFC+GEC scheme via
    fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual_ekfc() and packs the 47-byte
    PORT_ID-prefixed key via dual_lane_pid.

If a confirmed-arriving matching v6 frame HITS under install_v6pid,
the comparator needs a genuine nonzero EKFC known field (not GEC
content) to see a GEC-sourced composite, and VLAN-v6 should always
carry PORT_ID (or another known field) alongside the GEC lanes. If it
STILL misses, the gap is elsewhere and EKFC-vs-GEC sourcing is ruled
out.

Depends on fixup F_238.py (bin/kernel-fixups/, adds gec_keep_ekfc to
struct keygen_scheme and fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual_ekfc() to
fman_pcd_kg.c) having run; F_238 itself depends on F_236 (dual-lane
GEC opt-in). Verified via ~/kernel-git-cache/linux (canonical,
series-through-0187 + F-236/F-238 fixups applied) + git apply --check
against a fresh HEAD checkout. NOT YET BOARD-TESTED. Board sequence:
capture_init (sink fqid), then on a sacrificial port: "install_v6pid
<port> 17 <src6> <dst6> <sport> <dport> <sink-fqid-hex>", drive one
real matching IPv6 UDP packet from a real peer, check dmesg for
"oh_test capture: frame #1 ...". Then "clear <port>" + capture_fini.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate | Risk-Tier: B (new debug-only cc_test
verb + a new opt-in install path field, default false; no change to
any existing verb or production path)
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c      | 83 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 .../ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc_test.c         | 104 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h                           | 24 +++++++
 3 files changed, 209 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c
index e4dc3035c98b..cfaba7ee2c70 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c
@@ -377,6 +377,81 @@ static void cc_pack_key_dual(void __iomem *match, u16 idx,
 	memcpy_toio((void __iomem *)(row + CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL), msk, CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL);
 }
 
+/*
+ * T-M6-8 VLAN-v6 V6-2c: dual-lane key with a leading PORT_ID byte, for use
+ * with fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual_ekfc() (F-238) -- the isolating
+ * experiment testing whether the CC-tree comparator needs a real nonzero
+ * EKFC known field to see a GEC-sourced composite. With EKFC=0x80000000
+ * (KG_SCH_KN_PORT_ID alone), "generic extracts APPEND after known EKFC
+ * fields" (vendor source) means the silicon composite is the SAME
+ * cc_pack_key_dual() content, just ONE BYTE WIDER: PORT_ID first (0x00,
+ * deterministic on this ucode -- F-183/F-190, F-179 zeroes kgse_dv0/dv1),
+ * then the identical 46-byte dual-lane layout shifted by +1.
+ *
+ * cc_pack_key_dual() itself is untouched by this -- this is a separate,
+ * additive function so the already board-proven (register-writes-correct)
+ * all-GEC path keeps working exactly as before regardless of this
+ * experiment's outcome.
+ */
+#define CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID	(CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL + 1)
+
+static void cc_pack_key_dual_pid(void __iomem *match, u16 idx,
+				 const struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key *k)
+{
+	u8 key[CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID];
+	u8 msk[CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID];
+	u8 *row;
+	bool is_v6 = !!(k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_IPV6);
+
+	memset(key, 0, sizeof(key));
+	memset(msk, 0, sizeof(msk));
+
+	/* byte 0: PORT_ID, deterministically 0x00 on this ucode. */
+	msk[0] = 0xff;
+
+	key[1] = is_v6 ? CC_KEY_DUAL_FAMILY_V6 : CC_KEY_DUAL_FAMILY_V4;
+	msk[1] = 0xff;
+
+	if (is_v6) {
+		if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_IP) {
+			memcpy(&key[10], k->src_ip6, 16);
+			memset(&msk[10], 0xff, 16);
+		}
+		if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_IP) {
+			memcpy(&key[26], k->dst_ip6, 16);
+			memset(&msk[26], 0xff, 16);
+		}
+	} else {
+		if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_IP) {
+			memcpy(&key[2], &k->src_ip_be, 4);
+			msk[2] = msk[3] = msk[4] = msk[5] = 0xff;
+		}
+		if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_IP) {
+			memcpy(&key[6], &k->dst_ip_be, 4);
+			msk[6] = msk[7] = msk[8] = msk[9] = 0xff;
+		}
+	}
+
+	if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_PROTO) {
+		key[42] = k->proto;
+		msk[42] = 0xff;
+	}
+	if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_PORT) {
+		key[43] = (u8)(k->src_port_be & 0xff);
+		key[44] = (u8)(k->src_port_be >> 8);
+		msk[43] = msk[44] = 0xff;
+	}
+	if (k->present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_PORT) {
+		key[45] = (u8)(k->dst_port_be & 0xff);
+		key[46] = (u8)(k->dst_port_be >> 8);
+		msk[45] = msk[46] = 0xff;
+	}
+
+	row = (u8 __force *)match + (size_t)idx * 2 * CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID;
+	memcpy_toio((void __iomem *)row, key, CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID);
+	memcpy_toio((void __iomem *)(row + CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID), msk, CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID);
+}
+
 /*
  * Encode one leaf (result) action descriptor at AD row @idx - SDK-convergent
  * RESULT AD (0115; SDK FillAdOfTypeResult, sdk_fm_cc.c:2227-2343).
@@ -550,7 +625,9 @@ int fman_pcd_cc_static_install(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 port_id,
 	t->pcd = pcd;
 	t->port_id = port_id;
 	t->num_keys = hw->num_keys;
-	t->key_size = hw->dual_lane ? CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL : CC_KEY_SIZE;
+	t->key_size = hw->dual_lane ?
+		(hw->dual_lane_pid ? CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID : CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL) :
+		CC_KEY_SIZE;
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&t->node);
 
 	/* (num_keys + 1) rows: trailing row is the miss slot (RM 8.7.4.2/3). */
@@ -591,7 +668,9 @@ int fman_pcd_cc_static_install(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 port_id,
 
 	/* Encode each key's match record + leaf result AD. */
 	for (i = 0; i < hw->num_keys; i++) {
-		if (hw->dual_lane)
+		if (hw->dual_lane && hw->dual_lane_pid)
+			cc_pack_key_dual_pid(t->match, i, &hw->keys[i]);
+		else if (hw->dual_lane)
 			cc_pack_key_dual(t->match, i, &hw->keys[i]);
 		else
 			cc_pack_key(t->match, i, &hw->keys[i]);
diff --git a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
index 76b9db9c6979..91ab749a6785 100644
--- a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
+++ b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
@@ -288,6 +288,21 @@ int fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 hw_port_id,
 int fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 hw_port_id,
 				    u32 cc_group_off);
 
+/**
+ * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual_ekfc() - like
+ * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual(), but leaves KGSE_EKFC set to
+ * KG_SCH_KN_PORT_ID (0x80000000) instead of zeroing it (T-M6-8 VLAN-v6
+ * V6-2c, F-238 isolating experiment: does the CC-tree comparator need a
+ * real nonzero EKFC known field, not just GEC content, to see a
+ * GEC-sourced composite?). Pairs with struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec.dual_lane
+ * + a tree installed via cc_pack_key_dual_pid()'s 47-byte PORT_ID-prefixed
+ * layout -- NOT plain cc_pack_key_dual().
+ *
+ * Return: same as fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc().
+ */
+int fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual_ekfc(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 hw_port_id,
+					 u32 cc_group_off);
+
 /**
  * fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_cc() - restore an RX port's RSS scheme to the
  * plain BMI-enqueue path (reverse of fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc()).
@@ -513,6 +528,15 @@ struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec {
 			 * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc()) or the extracted key
 			 * width won't match what this tree compares.
 			 */
+	bool dual_lane_pid;	/* T-M6-8 VLAN-v6 V6-2c: like @dual_lane, but
+				 * packs the 47-byte PORT_ID-prefixed layout
+				 * (cc_pack_key_dual_pid(), CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID)
+				 * for use with a scheme armed via
+				 * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual_ekfc(). Ignored
+				 * unless @dual_lane is also set; @dual_lane alone
+				 * (this false) keeps the plain 46-byte
+				 * cc_pack_key_dual() path byte-identical.
+				 */
 };
 
 /**
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc_test.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc_test.c
index 81e3b7d6a2b1..bfede5f6417a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc_test.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc_test.c
@@ -436,6 +436,106 @@ static int cc_test_install_v4gec(struct fman_pcd *pcd, const char *args)
 	return err;
 }
 
+/*
+ * install_v6pid <port> <proto> <src-ip6> <dst-ip6> <sport> <dport> <fqid-hex>
+ *
+ * T-M6-8 VLAN-v6 V6-2c hybrid EKFC+GEC isolating experiment (F-238,
+ * 2026-09-02, after install_v6/install_v4gec's family-independent MISS):
+ * install_v6 and install_v4gec both proved an all-GEC (EKFC=0) composite
+ * is invisible to the CC-tree comparator, regardless of family. This verb
+ * tests the other half of that finding -- keep KGSE_EKFC nonzero
+ * (KG_SCH_KN_PORT_ID alone, 0x80000000) instead of zeroing it, via
+ * fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual_ekfc() (F-238), and pack the matching
+ * 47-byte PORT_ID-prefixed key via cc_pack_key_dual_pid()
+ * (spec->dual_lane_pid). If a real matching v6 frame HITS here, the
+ * comparator needs a genuine nonzero EKFC known field, not GEC content, to
+ * see a GEC-sourced composite -- and the fix for VLAN-v6 is to always
+ * carry PORT_ID (or another known field) alongside the GEC lanes. If it
+ * STILL misses, the gap is elsewhere (not an EKFC-vs-GEC sourcing issue).
+ */
+static int cc_test_install_v6pid(struct fman_pcd *pcd, const char *args)
+{
+	struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec *spec = NULL;
+	struct fman_port *rxport;
+	struct fman *fm;
+	char src_str[48], dst_str[48];
+	u8 src6[16], dst6[16];
+	u32 fqid, cc_base;
+	u8 port_id, proto;
+	u16 sport, dport;
+	int n, err;
+
+	n = sscanf(args, "install_v6pid %hhi %hhu %47s %47s %hu %hu %x",
+		   &port_id, &proto, src_str, dst_str, &sport, &dport, &fqid);
+	if (n != 7 || port_id >= ARRAY_SIZE(cc_test_vlan_hm) ||
+	    !(proto == 6 || proto == 17) || !fqid)
+		return -EINVAL;
+	if (in6_pton(src_str, -1, src6, -1, NULL) <= 0 ||
+	    in6_pton(dst_str, -1, dst6, -1, NULL) <= 0)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	fm = fman_pcd_get_fman(pcd);
+	if (!fm)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	spec = kzalloc(sizeof(*spec), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!spec)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	spec->num_keys = 1;
+	spec->miss_qband = 0;
+	spec->miss_fqid = 0;	/* miss stays on the existing RSS/SW path */
+	spec->dual_lane = true;
+	spec->dual_lane_pid = true;
+	spec->keys[0].present = FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_IPV6 |
+			       FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_PROTO |
+			       FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_IP |
+			       FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_IP |
+			       FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_PORT |
+			       FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_PORT;
+	spec->keys[0].proto = proto;
+	memcpy(spec->keys[0].src_ip6, src6, 16);
+	memcpy(spec->keys[0].dst_ip6, dst6, 16);
+	spec->keys[0].src_port_be = cpu_to_be16(sport);
+	spec->keys[0].dst_port_be = cpu_to_be16(dport);
+	spec->keys[0].target_qband = 0;
+	spec->keys[0].target_fqid = fqid;
+	spec->keys[0].hm_handle = 0;
+
+	err = fman_pcd_cc_static_install(pcd, port_id, spec);
+	kfree(spec);
+	if (err)
+		return err;
+
+	err = fman_pcd_cc_static_get_base(pcd, port_id, &cc_base);
+	if (err)
+		goto out_destroy_cc;
+	rxport = fman_port_lookup_rx(fm, port_id);
+	if (!rxport) {
+		err = -ENODEV;
+		goto out_destroy_cc;
+	}
+	err = fman_pcd_port_ensure_params_page(pcd, rxport);
+	if (err)
+		goto out_destroy_cc;
+	err = fman_port_set_cc_base(rxport, cc_base);
+	if (err)
+		goto out_destroy_cc;
+	err = fman_pcd_kg_port_attach_cc_dual_ekfc(pcd, port_id, cc_base);
+	if (err) {
+		(void)fman_port_set_cc_base(rxport, 0);
+		goto out_destroy_cc;
+	}
+
+	pr_info("fman_pcd cc_test: IPv6 dual-lane+PID (hybrid EKFC+GEC) port 0x%02x CC base 0x%x -> fqid 0x%x %pI6c:%u -> %pI6c:%u proto %u\n",
+		port_id, cc_base, fqid, src6, sport, dst6, dport, proto);
+	return 0;
+
+out_destroy_cc:
+	(void)fman_pcd_kg_port_detach_cc(pcd, port_id);
+	fman_pcd_cc_static_destroy(pcd, port_id);
+	return err;
+}
+
 /*
  * install_vlan <port> <proto> <src-ip> <dst-ip> <sport> <dport>
  *              <target-fqid-hex> <pop|push> <vid> [tpid-hex] [pcp]
@@ -805,6 +905,10 @@ static ssize_t cc_test_write(struct file *file, const char __user *buf,
 		ret = cc_test_install_v4gec(pcd, kbuf);
 		if (ret == 0)
 			ret = count;
+	} else if (strncmp(kbuf, "install_v6pid ", 14) == 0) {
+		ret = cc_test_install_v6pid(pcd, kbuf);
+		if (ret == 0)
+			ret = count;
 	} else if (strncmp(kbuf, "install_vlan ", 13) == 0) {
 		ret = cc_test_install_vlan(pcd, kbuf);
 		if (ret == 0)
